  "text": "ordinarium.praefatio-epiphaniae",
  "about": "The Preface of the Epiphany of the Lord. It praises the Only-begotten Son, Who appeared in our mortal nature and renewed us by the light of His immortality.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "Then the priest separates his hands and holds them apart until the end of the Preface. When it is finished, he joins them again and, bowing, says: Sanctus." },
    "s02": { "translation": "It is truly meet and just, right and profitable for salvation, that we should at all times and in all places give thanks unto Thee:" },
    "s03": { "translation": "O holy Lord, Father almighty, eternal God:" },
    "s04": { "translation": "For when Thine only-begotten Son appeared in the substance of our mortality, He renewed us by the new light of His immortality." },
    "s05": { "translation": "And therefore with Angels and Archangels, with Thrones and Dominions, and with all the hosts of the heavenly army, we sing the hymn of Thy glory, evermore saying:" }
  },
